d."]}, "overview": "Utah's first district became substantially more Democratic after redistricting, and the open-seat contest reflects that shift. Ben McAdams enters with a large financial advantage, having raised roughly $2.8 million and drawn $2.7 million in outside support, while Riley Owen has raised about $164,000. A September poll of likely voters put McAdams ahead 63 to 21, and prediction markets on both Kalshi and Polymarket give him roughly a 96 percent chance of winning.\n\nThe campaign has centered on cost-of-living and AI policy, with debates framing both candidates as moderates. Republican hopes of competing in the state's bluest corner appear in coverage, but there is little evidence of traction: no opposing outside spending, no expert ratings treating the race as competitive, and polling, fundraising, and the district's lean all pointing the same way. The district leans Democratic by about 12 points, and the national environment adds to that edge.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9908, "margin": 20.9}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.99, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9893, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9909, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9895, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9899, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9906, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9886, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9895, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9907, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.99, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9979, "margin": 28.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9958, "margin": 26.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.997, "margin": 27.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9991, "margin": 28.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9988, "margin": 27.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9979, "margin": 27.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.9971, "marg